# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Pages INHERITS the headers of every matching rule and JOINS duplicate
# header names with a comma, so a Cache-Control set under /* is never
# overridden by /assets/* - it is appended to it. A rule for /assets/*
# that only *adds* Cache-Control therefore produces the broken value
# "no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable"
# (no-store wins, nothing is cached). Prefix the name with "! " to detach
# the inherited value first, then set the one we want.

# HTML is the only thing that must never go stale after a deployment, so the
# no-store policy stays on the catch-all and is detached for long-lived assets.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# Long-lived media: content-hashed copies live in /assets/hash/ (see
# make_assets_hashed.py) and originals keep their canonical, crawler-facing
# URLs. The detached Cache-Control replaces the inherited no-store policy
# instead of colliding with it; `immutable` is safe now that every rendered
# reference embeds the hash of the bytes being served.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
